|WKB                          QUEST COMMANDS
|CKB=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=

|YKOThe following commands are available for managing quests:

  |YKBqlist |WKB[filter]
    |YKOLists all available quests. Quests are color-coded by difficulty
    relative to your level. You can filter by domain, level, deity,
    reputation, type, tag, or status.

    |YKOExamples:
      |YKBqlist darkwind
      |YKBqlist level 1-10
      |YKBqlist deity set
      |YKBqlist rep villain
      |YKBqlist type kill
      |YKBqlist available

  |YKBqinfo |WKB<number>
    |YKODisplays full details for a quest: its description, level range,
    area hint, quest points, reputation/deity tags, rewards, and a
    list of objectives.

  |YKBqaccept |WKB<number>
    |YKOAccepts a quest using its number from |YKBqlist|YKO. Suggested
    levels are guidance, not requirements, but prerequisite quests still
    apply. You cannot accept a quest you have already completed or accepted.
    |YKBqinfo |YKOand |YKBqaccept |YKOuse the most recent |YKBqlist |YKOresult, so
    filtered quest numbers stay stable.

  |YKBqactive |WKB<number>
    |YKOThis command is kept for compatibility. Active quests are no
    longer needed; all accepted quests track progress automatically.

  |YKBmyquests
    |YKOLists all quests you have accepted, showing which one is active
    and the current status of each.

  |YKBqstatus
    |YKOShows detailed progress reports for your accepted unfinished quests,
    including each objective and how much you have completed. You can use
    |YKBqstatus <number> |YKOwith numbers from |YKBmyquests|YKO.

  |YKBescort
    |YKOBegins an escort sequence if one of your accepted quests has an escort
    objective. The NPC will start moving and you must follow and
    protect them.

|CKB=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=
|WKBSee also: |YKBhelp quests, help quests objectives
